model {
  extend basalt.toolsGateway {
    metadata {
      constraint "The member allowance for invitation acceptance and SSO membership reads an existing billing customer read-only. Each read attempt gets eight seconds, and a hung attempt, transport failure, server error or rate limit gets at most two more with jittered backoff; the reads and any creation share the single ten-second budget one billing write has. Only a definitive customer-not-found answer creates the customer, and that write is sent once and never retried. An unconfirmed allowance fails closed and is never unlimited. The refusal keeps the person-facing message and adds only a fixed code, the billing operation, failure reason, provider HTTP status and a reference that the server warning log also records next to the billing customer; provider bodies, credentials and endpoints never leave the billing adapter. The mapping lives in the shared auth core that every Cloud auth entry builds on, so invitation and SSO admissions report the same safe fields."
    }
  }
}
